jstone@hotcity.UUCP (John Stone) writes:
 Since I started reading this newgroup, I keep seeing the phrase polypiling(sp)
 come up.  Would some one explain what this is?  I haven't the slightest idea
 of what it is other than a way to cheat.

You obviously haven't played enough, or you'd have figured this out
already.  Anyway...

It's not cheating.  It can make some games much easier.  It's a way to
drive up your score.  It can also change an iffy (no shops, no altars,
no nuthin') game into a winable.  This last reason is the important one.

Really mild spoiler ahead


The idea is you take a pile of (useless) stuff, and zap it with a
polymorph spell (from a wand or by casting).  All the stuff changes into
new stuff.  You can then dig thru the pile and see if any of that new
stuff is useful.  Of course, this can be repeated until you run out of
polymorph spells.

